{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_overview_cluster_singleton", "label": "Cluster singleton", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One actor that exists exactly once cluster-wide. Singletons are not a low-latency-failover tool: they trade some unavailability during failover for uniqueness."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_overview_clustersingletonproxy", "label": "ClusterSingletonProxy", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "start and ref both hand back a plain forwarding ActorRef, so nothing in a consumer signature has to know it is a singleton."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_overview_singletonkey", "label": "SingletonKey", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A role belongs on the key: it is not part of the identity (two keys are equal iff their names match) but rides along so every node reads the same one \u2014 a node that only calls ref has no options object, so a role set only via withRole would be invisible and its proxy would resolve a different host than the managers."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_overview_start_vs_ref", "label": "start() versus ref()", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "start puts the node into rotation, ref only addresses. ref.stop() is a warning no-op because elsewhere stop() sends a PoisonPill, which here would kill whatever the current leader is hosting."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_overview_buffersize", "label": "Proxy bufferSize", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Bounds what the proxy holds while the cluster has no host; past the default 1000 messages go to dead letters rather than growing the buffer forever. The buffer drains on the first cluster event that can have produced a host, not only a leader change."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_overview_failover_sequence", "label": "Failover sequence", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Detection, election, hand-over, spawn, routing shift. How strong the uniqueness is depends on configuration: without a lease it holds only while the outgoing host can be reached and answers."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_overview_warm_handover", "label": "Warm hand-over", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "For state expensive to rebuild but cheap to copy: persistence makes state survive but does not make the successor fast. restoreFromHandOver runs after the constructor and before preStart, the only position from which recovery can still be skipped. It is allowed not to happen and falls back to a cold start with a warn."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_overview_warmhandoveractor", "label": "WarmHandOverActor", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Opted into on the actor, not in the options \u2014 there is no flag; serializeForHandOver is called after postStop so the snapshot is final, and an instance that died to a crash is never asked."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_overview_handover_snapshot_cap", "label": "Hand-over snapshot cap (1 MiB)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The snapshot travels while the singleton is running nowhere, so a very large one lengthens the outage instead of shortening it; base64 in a JSON frame costs about a third more, and one that would not fit maxFrameBytes is refused because an oversized frame costs the whole inter-node connection."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_overview_no_singletonactor_interface", "label": "No SingletonActor interface, deliberately", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "TypeScript's implements constrains only the instance side \u2014 there is no static implements \u2014 so a marker interface would be structurally empty. A static field composes with any base class, which matters because a singleton is frequently also a PersistentActor."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_overview_singleton_cost", "label": "Cost of a singleton", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A manager on every node, a proxy hop on every tell, and unavailability for the seconds it takes the cluster to converge on a new leader; if N replicas would do, a cluster router or sharding scales horizontally with no leader bottleneck."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_overview_split_brain_defenses", "label": "Split-brain defenses", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A downing strategy picks a winning side; a lease moves arbitration to a third party. Downing plus lease is paranoid-safe; each alone is usually enough."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_overview_persistent_warm_start_sequence", "label": "Warm start and the journal sequence number", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A warm-started PersistentActor holds state that never came from a replay, so its sequence number has to travel in the snapshot too; otherwise its first persist writes at a position the journal has used, which fencing correctly reads as a second writer."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_overview_cluster_singleton", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_overview_clustersingletonproxy", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_overview_cluster_singleton", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_overview_singletonkey", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_overview_cluster_singleton", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_overview_start_vs_ref", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_overview_clustersingletonproxy", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_overview_buffersize", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_overview_cluster_singleton", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_overview_failover_sequence", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_overview_failover_sequence", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_overview_warm_handover", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_overview_warm_handover", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_overview_warmhandoveractor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_overview_warm_handover", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_overview_handover_snapshot_cap", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/overview.mdx", "source_location": 